{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Here I am against you</b> — Nineveh." "<b>In smoke</b> — from the great heat of the fire. And the meaning concerns the wrath of HaShem." "<b>Your prey</b> — the prey that you used to snatch. And the heh of מלאככה serves in place of the yod as a feminine suffix marker, like עוניכי תחלואיכי. And the meaning is Rabshakeh, as written: 'by the hand of Your angels.'"], :book :nahum, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {2 "The reference to Rabshakeh and the citation 'ביד מלאכיך' (2 Kings 19:35) is cryptic; Ibn Ezra appears to hint that Assyria's appointed angel is destroyed. Translated hyper-literally without expanding the argument. The word מלאככה is ambiguous in the manuscript and could mean 'your angel' or relate to the feminine suffix discussion; rendered as found."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Nahum -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/nachum"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:14:40.121789917Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}